      "explanation": ". > ~\n\nThe largest compliaice i in the cifetlatory system is of veins.\n\nVascular eompliance/eapacitanice i is the total quantity of blood that can be stored in a given\nportion of the circulation for each mmHg pressure rise.\n\nVascular Compliance = distensibility X volume.\n\nThe compliance of a systemic vein is about 24 times that of its corresponding artery because it is\nabout 8 times as distensible and has a volume about 3 times as artery (8 x 3 = 24)."
    },
