      ],
      "explanation": "The Bernoulli's theorem states that in a tube or blood vessel, the sum of the kinetic energy of flow\nand pressure energy is constant.\n\nOther options:\n\n+ Option B: Travelling wave theory (Theories of hearing): Low tones produce maximum\nstimulation at the apex of the cochlea.\n\n475, \n\n* Option C: Weber—Fechner law: The magnitude of sensation felt is proportional to the log of the\nintensity of the stimulus.\n\n* Option D: Frank—Starling law of the heart: Force of contraction is proportional to stretch of the\ncardiac muscle."
    },
