      ],
      "explanation": "Inferior vena cava has the highest oxygen concentration in fetal circulation.\n\nThe blood gets oxygenated in the placenta and this passes to the umbilical vein. From the\numbilical vein, 50% of the blood enters the hepatic circulation and 50% bypasses the liver to enter\nthe inferior vena cava. From here, the blood enters the heart via the right atrium. The right atrium\nalso receives deoxygenated blood from the superior vena cava. This mixed blood is distributed to\nthe body via aorta. e@\n\nTherefore, inferior vena cava has the highest concentration of oxygen in the fetal Girculation.\n\nvy"
